From: Trae <trae@example.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: ov13b10: Fix ACPI PM handling for device-tree systems

The OV13B10 driver uses acpi_dev_state_d0() to determine if full power
initialization should be performed during probe. On device-tree based systems
(non-ACPI), this function always returns false, causing the sensor to skip
power-on and chip identification during probe.

This patch modifies the logic to:
1. Check if the system is ACPI or device-tree based
2. Force full power initialization for device-tree systems

This ensures that the rear camera (OV13B10) on Xiaomi Pad 6 (Pipa) is properly
powered and identified during probe, allowing it to register with the media
controller and libcamera.

---
 drivers/media/i2c/ov13b10.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/ov13b10.c b/drivers/media/i2c/ov13b10.c
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov13b10.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov13b10.c
@@ -1712,6 +1712,13 @@ static int ov13b10_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 		return ret;
 
 	full_power = acpi_dev_state_d0(ov13b->dev);
+
+	/* For device-tree based systems, acpi_dev_state_d0() always returns false.
+	 * We need to force full power initialization on such systems to ensure
+	 * the sensor is properly powered and identified during probe.
+	 */
+	if (!ACPI_COMPANION(ov13b->dev))
+		full_power = true;  /* Force power-on for device-tree systems */
 	/* #region debug-point ov13b10-probe */
 	dev_dbg(ov13b->dev, "ov13b10-debug: probe full_power=%d\n", full_power);
 	/* #endregion debug-point ov13b10-probe */
